2.25.1

        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.
        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.

        Root cause:
        The bug was caused by the declaration of the variable `shProg` being placed after its usage within several functions in `uniforms.c`. This led to MSVC compiler errors indicating that `shProg` was undeclared at the point of its use, as well as syntax errors due to the improper order of declarations and code execution. C requires that variables be declared before they are used, which was not adhered to in the original code.

        Commit message:
        mesa: Move declarations before code.

This patch fixes these MSVC build errors introduced with
73b78f9c9f86dd38fb165f4730aeac9519635b07.

